  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "narration": "Can a ball be in two places at the same time? In the tiny world... yes.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Two places\n*at once?*",
          "at": "can",
          "x": 540,
          "y": 600,
          "size": 190
        },
        {
          "type": "drawing",
          "drawing": "TwoBalls",
          "at": "same",
          "duration": 2.2,
          "x": 540,
          "y": 1120,
          "width": 860,
          "height": 470
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "top",
      "narration": "Imagine a spinning top, whirling super fast, in the dark. Is it spinning up, or down? You can't tell. As long as it's dark, it's a bit of both at the same time. But when you switch on the light and look at it... pop! It picks just one direction. Tiny things, like electrons, do exactly that.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "drawing",
          "drawing": "Spinner",
          "at": "top",
          "duration": 2.0,
          "x": 330,
          "y": 760,
          "width": 380,
          "height": 530
        },
        {
          "type": "drawing",
          "drawing": "MotionLines",
          "at": "fast",
          "duration": 1.3,
          "out": "pop",
          "x": 330,
          "y": 740,
          "width": 600,
          "height": 470
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "↑ or ↓ ?",
          "at": "spinning#2",
          "out": "pop",
          "x": 820,
          "y": 520,
          "size": 140,
          "cps": 6
        },
        {
          "type": "drawing",
          "drawing": "LightBulb",
          "at": "switch",
          "duration": 1.2,
          "then": "light",
          "x": 820,
          "y": 980,
          "width": 380,
          "height": 450
        },
        {
          "type": "drawing",
          "drawing": "Arrow",
          "props": {
            "direction": "up"
          },
          "at": "picks",
          "duration": 0.7,
          "x": 330,
          "y": 360,
          "width": 110,
          "height": 230,
          "color": "yellow"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "*electron* = spinning top",
          "at": "electrons",
          "x": 540,
          "y": 1440,
          "size": 104
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge",
      "narration": "Okay. Now let's see how physicists say it.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "How physicists\nsay it",
          "at": "okay",
          "x": 540,
          "y": 820,
          "size": 160,
          "cps": 18
        },
        {
          "type": "drawing",
          "drawing": "Underline",
          "props": {
            "count": 2
          },
          "at": "say",
          "duration": 0.8,
          "x": 540,
          "y": 1035,
          "width": 720,
          "height": 90,
          "color": "yellow"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "physics",
      "narration": "Before it's measured, an electron is in a superposition of states: it's our top, spinning both ways at once. This situation is described by a wave function, which tells us the probability of finding it in each state. When we measure it, the wave function collapses, and the electron takes on a single state. That's the light switching on.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "*SUPERPOSITION*",
          "at": "superposition",
          "x": 540,
          "y": 200,
          "size": 120,
          "cps": 20
        },
        {
          "type": "drawing",
          "drawing": "Arrow",
          "props": {
            "direction": "down"
          },
          "at": "our",
          "duration": 0.5,
          "x": 200,
          "y": 330,
          "width": 70,
          "height": 130
        },
        {
          "type": "drawing",
          "drawing": "Spinner",
          "at": "top",
          "duration": 1.0,
          "x": 210,
          "y": 510,
          "width": 150,
          "height": 210
        },
        {
          "type": "drawing",
          "drawing": "MotionLines",
          "at": "both",
          "duration": 0.6,
          "x": 210,
          "y": 505,
          "width": 260,
          "height": 200
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "(the top in the dark)",
          "at": "once",
          "x": 650,
          "y": 500,
          "size": 72
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Wave function = *probability*",
          "at": "wave",
          "x": 540,
          "y": 740,
          "size": 84,
          "cps": 18
        },
        {
          "type": "drawing",
          "drawing": "Wave",
          "at": "probability",
          "duration": 1.6,
          "x": 540,
          "y": 900,
          "width": 820,
          "height": 220
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "*MEASURE → COLLAPSE*",
          "at": "measure",
          "x": 540,
          "y": 1100,
          "size": 104,
          "cps": 18
        },
        {
          "type": "drawing",
          "drawing": "Wave",
          "props": {
            "axis": true
          },
          "at": "collapses",
          "duration": 0.7,
          "then": "single",
          "thenDuration": 0.9,
          "x": 600,
          "y": 1265,
          "width": 640,
          "height": 190
        },
        {
          "type": "drawing",
          "drawing": "Arrow",
          "props": {
            "direction": "down"
          },
          "at": "light",
          "duration": 0.4,
          "x": 150,
          "y": 1270,
          "width": 70,
          "height": 220
        },
        {
          "type": "drawing",
          "drawing": "LightBulb",
          "props": {
            "lit": true
          },
          "at": "light",
          "delay": 0.3,
          "duration": 0.9,
          "x": 170,
          "y": 1490,
          "width": 200,
          "height": 230
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
